From: Not-a-dude <honkhonkovic842@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wlserver: associate spi touchscreens with internal monitor

Touchscreens on mobile Snapdragon platforms (such as Focaltech FT8756)
are connected over the SPI bus instead of I2C. Include the "spi"
subsystem in the internal monitor heuristic so touch is properly associated
and rotated according to panel orientation.
---
 src/wlserver.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/wlserver.cpp b/src/wlserver.cpp
--- a/src/wlserver.cpp
+++ b/src/wlserver.cpp
@@ -470,7 +470,7 @@ static void wlserver_touch_associate_connector(struct wlserver_touch *touch)
 	while (parent) {
 		const char *subsystem = udev_device_get_subsystem(parent);
 		if (subsystem) {
-			if (strcmp( subsystem, "i2c" ) == 0) {
+			if (strcmp( subsystem, "i2c" ) == 0 || strcmp( subsystem, "spi" ) == 0) {
 				connector = GetBackend()->GetConnector(gamescope::GAMESCOPE_SCREEN_TYPE_INTERNAL);
 				break;
 			} else if (strcmp( subsystem, "usb" ) == 0) {
-- 
